From a9f17733e5e019c460d5b25f28d638e5f803efe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:39:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/39] board: zte: add the shared slot core and the slot
 writer

The E4 v2 rescue must be able to install a firmware package into a slot
without duplicating what the Linux e2631-fwslot tool does.  This adds a
self-contained slot core (header layout, package parsing, identity and
guard rules, CRC32) that the host test also compiles, plus a thin MTD
writer around it:

  - e2631_slotcore.[ch] is plain C over linux/types.h, shared byte for
    byte with tests/native/uboot/ in the kit;
  - e2631fwslot.[ch] scans and verifies the two slots the way cspboot and
    e2631-fwslot do, refuses to replace a working vendor system, erases
    the whole target slot, programs the body in erase blocks, stamps and
    writes the version header after it, then reads the slot back and
    erases the header if the read-back does not match.

The writer is the only module allowed to program a slot; mtd0 stays with
e2631flash and the environment block with e2631env.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
